Package: hkselect
Title: Selecting Housekeeper Genes with Heteroscedastic Linear Models (Szabo et al. 2004)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("fossil contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "noreply@github.com")
Description: The statistical models of Szabo, Perou, Karaca, Perreard, Palais, Quackenbush and
    Bernard (2004, Genome Biology 5:R59, <doi:10.1186/gb-2004-5-8-r59>) for choosing
    housekeeper (reference) genes for normalizing quantitative RT-PCR data. Within one tissue
    type, a two-way model of log expression with one error variance per gene (Model 1a) gives
    each gene's standard deviation and the standard deviation of the log geometric mean of any
    gene set. Across tissue types, a model with a tissue-specific gene effect and errors whose
    standard deviation is a gene factor times a tissue factor (Model 2) gives each gene's bias
    and variance per tissue type, and a minimax mean squared error search finds the best
    universal set of each size. Also Vandesompele's geNorm M-values for comparison. Rebuilt from
    the paper's text; the authors' code was never released.
